{"subject":"Biochemistry","sourceTitle":"All In One Online","title":"PrepLadder · 27.Previous Year Questions","deckName":"created by tele @Neet_pg_bot::prep::Qbank::Biochemistry::27.Previous_Year_Questions","questions":[{"id":"all-in-one-1760436512890","topic":"PrepLadder · 27.Previous Year Questions","number":1,"stem":"Heme is derived from which of the following amino acids?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Glutamine"},{"label":"B","text":"Glycine"},{"label":"C","text":"Glutamate"},{"label":"D","text":"Valine"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Glycine","solutionHtml":"succinyl-CoA in the first step of <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d4fff554a316927771885dc8700abe\">heme</span> synthesis, catalyzed by the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"0f160e4e42169277718771b715516a\">enzyme</span> δ-aminolevulinic acid<strong> (ALA) synthase</strong>. This reaction is the <strong>rate-limiting step</strong> in <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d4fff554a316927771885dc8700abe\">heme</span> biosynthesis.\n<p style=\"text-align:center\"><img alt=\"Porphyria classification\" data-author=\"\" data-hash=\"13013\" data-license=\"\" data-source=\"\" data-tags=\"May2025\" height=\"600\" src=\"images/exp_104_103_1.jpg\" width=\"600\"/></p>\n<p><strong>Glutamine (Option A):</strong> Glutamine is involved in <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"94a2f0970016927771932885a3d362\">nucleotide</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"859a34e1061692777183872a5e4441\">biosynthesis</span> and <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"edbc0adbb31692777181ed0ee792d4\">ammonia</span> transport but does not play a direct role in <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d4fff554a316927771885dc8700abe\">heme</span> synthesis.</p>\n<p><strong>Glutamate (Option C): </strong>Glutamate is primarily involved in the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"3fda45538a1692777199ec2a5478a5\">synthesis</span> of <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"f945849e691692777188ad7ce5b5e2\">glutathione</span> and neurotransmitters but does not contribute to <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d4fff554a316927771885dc8700abe\">heme</span> synthesis.</p>\n<p><strong>Valine (Option D): </strong>Valine is a branched-chain <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"543f207eb51692777181723491a358\">amino</span> acid involved in protein <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"3fda45538a1692777199ec2a5478a5\">synthesis</span> and energy production but not in <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d4fff554a316927771885dc8700abe\">heme</span> biosynthesis.</p><br/><img src=\"images/exp_104_103_1.jpg\"/><br/><br/><div class=\"quiz-references\">Vasudevan Textbook of Biochemistry Edition 7th Pg. 271, 272, 273</div>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436512892","topic":"PrepLadder · 27.Previous Year Questions","number":2,"stem":"Which of the following amino acids are necessary for purine ring formation?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Glycine, aspartate, valine"},{"label":"B","text":"Glycine, Aspartate, Glutamine"},{"label":"C","text":"Glycine, Aspartate, Glutamate"},{"label":"D","text":"Glycine, Asparagine, Glutamine"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Glycine, Aspartate, Glutamine","solutionHtml":"a358\"&amp;gt;amino acids - <strong>Glycine, Aspartate, Glutamine </strong>and the <strong>cofactor N10-formyl <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"e50618732a1692777200a3c8dfc804\">tetrahydrofolate</span> (N10- <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"8df215e687169277720338b5552dd1\">formyl</span> THF)</strong> for <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"c03d9c910716927771961a9a2609b5\">purine</span> ring formation.\n<p><strong>(Option B)</strong><strong> (Option A, C and D ruled out)</strong></p>\n<p><img alt=\"BC075A Sources of purine ring\" data-author=\"\" data-hash=\"13082\" data-license=\"\" data-source=\"\" data-tags=\"May2025\" height=\"384\" src=\"images/exp_104_51_1.jpg\" width=\"600\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The sources of each <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"435060133416927771829458eecc80\">atom</span> in a <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"c03d9c910716927771961a9a2609b5\">purine</span> were found by <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"11a5eea407169277720251b8446fa7\">feeding</span> isotopic precursors of <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"ffa20262931692777201caef35de16\">uric</span> acid to pigeons.\n\t<ul>\n<li>The<strong> C-2 </strong>atom is from <strong>formyl THF</strong></li>\n<li>The<strong> C-8</strong> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"435060133416927771829458eecc80\">atom</span> is from <strong>N5N10 methenyl THF</strong></li>\n<li>The <strong>C-6</strong> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"435060133416927771829458eecc80\">atom</span> is from <strong>respiratory CO2</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>N1 </strong>is from aspartate</li>\n<li><strong>N3 </strong>and <strong>N9 </strong>are from <strong>Glutamine</strong></li>\n<li><strong>C4,</strong> <strong>C5 </strong>and <strong>N7 </strong>are from <strong>Glycine</strong></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul><br/><img src=\"images/exp_104_51_1.jpg\"/><br/><br/><div class=\"quiz-references\">https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7869020/<br/>Harper’s Illustrated Biochemistry, 32nd edition, pg:338, 339<br/>Vasudevan textbook of biochemistry, 7th edition, pg: 208</div>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436512894","topic":"PrepLadder · 27.Previous Year Questions","number":3,"stem":"Decreased % transferrin saturation is seen in?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Hemochromatosis"},{"label":"B","text":"Iron deficiency anemia"},{"label":"C","text":"Megaloblastic anemia"},{"label":"D","text":"Hemosiderosis"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Iron deficiency anemia","solutionHtml":":1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\"&amp;gt;\n\t\t\t<p>Hemoglobin Indices</p>\n\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Low Mean Corpuscular <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"ad2073fe6716927771885f3c1ec652\">Hemoglobin</span> (MCH), Low <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"26a767cc56169277719293a7e14090\">Mean Corpuscular Volume</span> (MCV)</p>\n</td>\n\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Peripheral Blood Smear</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Microcytosis, Hypochromia, Anisocytosis</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Serum Ferritin</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Decreased</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Serum Iron</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Decreased</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Transferrin Saturation</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Decreased</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Total Iron-Binding Capacity</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Increased</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Stool for <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"c8d9b6cbbb1692777194c4bc31f01f\">Occult</span> Blood</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>May be positive</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Mentzer Index</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>&amp;gt;15</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Hemoglobin Electrophoresis</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Normal</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Bone <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"c8a8c935a41692777191610f6aacb4\">Marrow</span> Aspiration/Biopsy</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Iron stores absent on staining</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>In the rest of the conditions, the % <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d404d819f41692777200b686a0759e\">transferrin</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"e4696a0f8d169277719865588e55c7\">saturation</span> is normal or increased</li>\n</ul>\n<p> </p><br/><br/><div class=\"quiz-references\">https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK448065/</div>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436512896","topic":"PrepLadder · 27.Previous Year Questions","number":4,"stem":"Which part of the haemoglobin molecule does 2,3-Bisphosphoglycerate (2,3-BPG) bind to in order to regulate oxygen release?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Alpha chains of haemoglobin"},{"label":"B","text":"Heme iron centre"},{"label":"C","text":"Beta chains of haemoglobin"},{"label":"D","text":"Globin-heme interface"}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Beta chains of haemoglobin","solutionHtml":"ong&amp;gt;Explanation:\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>2,3-BPG binds within the <strong>central cavity</strong> of the <strong>deoxyhaemoglobin tetramer</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>It interacts with <strong>positively charged residues</strong> (mainly <strong>lysine and histidine</strong>) on the <strong>β-chains</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>This binding <strong>stabilises the T (tense) state</strong>, <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"ff02aa40d51692777191246d4a9b87\">lowering</span> haemoglobin’s <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"227269f3ec1692777180d76a7898dd\">affinity</span> for oxygen and promoting oxygen delivery to tissues.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align:center\"><img alt=\"\" data-author=\"\" data-hash=\"\" data-license=\"\" data-source=\"\" data-tags=\"\" height=\"346\" src=\"images/exp_110_25_1.jpg\" width=\"916\"/></p>\n<p><strong>Effect of 2,3 BPG on Hb:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Reduces the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"227269f3ec1692777180d76a7898dd\">affinity</span> of Hb for oxygen and helps unload oxygen to tissues.</li>\n<li>A <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"1635abe5e5169277718365a15769c5\">by-product</span> of glycolysis. <strong>(Rapaport Leubering Cycle)</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><strong>Alpha chains of haemoglobin (Option A)</strong>:<br/>\nIncorrect because 2,3-BPG binds primarily to residues on the <strong>β-chains</strong>, not the α-chains.</p>\n<p><strong>Heme iron <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"1feb2a0a3016927771847db9449f75\">centre</span> (Option B)</strong>:<br/>\n2,3-BPG does <strong>not bind directly to <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d4fff554a316927771885dc8700abe\">heme</span> or iron</strong>; it acts <strong>allosterically</strong>, not at the active oxygen-binding site.</p>\n<p><strong>Globin-heme <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"ec503a687b16927771908fbd6d884c\">interface</span> (Option D)</strong>:<br/>\nThis is the site of <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"3820ba101416927771858fe257e119\">coordination</span> between <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"debd75cb191692777188288f956f22\">globin</span> and heme, not where 2,3-BPG binds.</p><br/><img src=\"images/exp_110_25_1.jpg\"/><br/><br/><div class=\"quiz-references\">Harper&rsquo;s Illustrated Biochemistry, 32nd Edition, Page 55</div>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436512898","topic":"PrepLadder · 27.Previous Year Questions","number":5,"stem":"What does iron deficiency anemia (IDA) stand for?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Low serum ferritin"},{"label":"B","text":"Low transferrin saturation"},{"label":"C","text":"Increased TIBC"},{"label":"D","text":"All of the above"}],"answer":"D","answerText":"All of the above","solutionHtml":"d #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\"&amp;gt;\n\t\t\t<p>Hemoglobin Indices</p>\n\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Low Mean Corpuscular <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"ad2073fe6716927771885f3c1ec652\">Hemoglobin</span> (MCH), Low <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"26a767cc56169277719293a7e14090\">Mean Corpuscular Volume</span> (MCV)</p>\n</td>\n\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Peripheral Blood Smear</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Microcytosis, Hypochromia, Anisocytosis</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Serum Ferritin</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Decreased</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Serum Iron</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Decreased</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Transferrin Saturation</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Decreased</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Total Iron-Binding Capacity</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Increased</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Stool for <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"c8d9b6cbbb1692777194c4bc31f01f\">Occult</span> Blood</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>May be positive</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Mentzer Index</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>&amp;gt;15</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Hemoglobin Electrophoresis</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Normal</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Bone <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"c8a8c935a41692777191610f6aacb4\">Marrow</span> Aspiration/Biopsy</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Iron stores absent on staining</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n\n<br/><br/><div class=\"quiz-references\">https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK448065/</div>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436512900","topic":"PrepLadder · 27.Previous Year Questions","number":6,"stem":"Which of the following is the rate-limiting enzyme of heme synthesis pathway?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"HMB synthase"},{"label":"B","text":"δ Amino-Levulinic Acid dehydratase"},{"label":"C","text":"δ Amino-Levulinic Acid synthase"},{"label":"D","text":"Ferrochelatase"}],"answer":"C","answerText":"δ Amino-Levulinic Acid synthase","solutionHtml":"/span&amp;gt; <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"3fda45538a1692777199ec2a5478a5\">synthesis</span> pathway. Its activity is tightly regulated by <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"a1c9a7400e1692777203b61723d426\">feedback inhibition</span> by <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d4fff554a316927771885dc8700abe\">heme</span> itself.\n\n<p> </p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center\"><img alt=\"Classification of Porphyrias\" data-author=\"\" data-hash=\"12823\" data-license=\"\" data-source=\"\" data-tags=\"May2025\" height=\"438\" src=\"images/exp_112_81_1.jpg\" width=\"600\"/></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><strong>Heme Synthesis:</strong></p>\n<table cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:612px\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:1px solid black; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Step</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:1px solid black; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Reaction</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:1px solid black; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Enzyme</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:1px solid black; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Location</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:1px solid black; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Key Points</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Succinyl CoA + <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"6df8c5de5016927771881dc6865f2e\">Glycine</span> → Delta-aminolevulinic acid (ALA)</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>ALA <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d2bd91ccac169277719941254e1795\">Synthase</span> <strong>(Option C)</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Mitochondria</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Rate-limiting step</strong>; requires <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"ad5806d5ad1692777196f1158adc4e\">pyridoxal</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"189b6fc834169277719580eb39bb4c\">phosphate</span> as a cofactor</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>2 ALA → Porphobilinogen (PBG)</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>ALA Dehydratase <strong>(Option B)</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Cytoplasm</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>It involves removal of 2 molecules of water; the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"0f160e4e42169277718771b715516a\">enzyme</span> contains <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"39ecb6e07416927772029550b7e74a\">zinc</span> and is inhibited by lead</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>4 PBG → Hydroxymethylbilane (HMB)</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Uroporphyrinogen I Synthase/ HMB <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d2bd91ccac169277719941254e1795\">synthase</span> <strong>(Option A)</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Cytoplasm</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>-</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>4a</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>HMB → Uroporphyrinogen I</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Spontaneous cyclization</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Cytoplasm</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>-</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>4b</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>HMB → Uroporphyrinogen III</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Uroporphyrinogen III Synthase</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Cytoplasm</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>-</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>5</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Uroporphyrinogen III → Coproporphyrinogen III</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Uroporphyrinogen Decarboxylase</p>\n<p> </p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Cytoplasm</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Decarboxylation, removal of 4 molecules of CO2</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>6</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Coproporphyrinogen III → Protoporphyrinogen III</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Coproporphyrinogen Oxidase</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Mitochondria</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p> </p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>7</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Protoporphyrinogen III → Protoporphyrin III</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Protoporphyrinogen Oxidase</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Mitochondria</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p> </p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>8</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Protoporphyrin III → Heme</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Ferrochelatase</p>\n<p><strong>(Option D)</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Mitochondria</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Insertion of Fe2+</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table><br/><img src=\"images/exp_112_81_1.jpg\"/><br/><br/><div class=\"quiz-references\">Vasudevan Textbook of Biochemistry Edition 7th Pg. 271, 272, 273</div>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436512902","topic":"PrepLadder · 27.Previous Year Questions","number":7,"stem":"A female was diagnosed with lead poisoning. What is the probable enzyme defect responsible for her condition?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"ALA synthase"},{"label":"B","text":"ALA dehydratase"},{"label":"C","text":"Heme synthase"},{"label":"D","text":"Coproporphyrinogen oxidase"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"ALA dehydratase","solutionHtml":"77196f21b086f92\"&amp;gt;poisoning can lead to <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"0f0b2969921692777180de24f0b0c0\">acquired</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"e5f770f89c16927771966b9e3da618\">porphyria</span> by inhibiting 3 enzymes of the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d4fff554a316927771885dc8700abe\">heme</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"3fda45538a1692777199ec2a5478a5\">synthesis</span> pathway:\n<table cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:624px\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:1px solid black; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Enzyme inhibited</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:1px solid black; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>ALA dehydratase<strong> (Primarily inhibited)</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>ALA elevation</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Coproporphyrinogen oxidase</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Coproporphyrin elevation</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Ferrochelatase</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Elevated <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"39ecb6e07416927772029550b7e74a\">Zinc</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"510ec2d8ea1692777196c492eae686\">protoporphyrin</span> levels<strong> (Most sensitive marker)</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p> </p>\n<p><strong>ALA <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d2bd91ccac169277719941254e1795\">synthase</span> (Option A)</strong> is an <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"0f160e4e42169277718771b715516a\">enzyme</span> involved in the first step of <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d4fff554a316927771885dc8700abe\">heme</span> synthesis, where delta-aminolevulinic acid (ALA) is formed.</p>\n<p><strong>Heme <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d2bd91ccac169277719941254e1795\">synthase</span> (Option C)</strong>, also known as ferrochelatase, is involved in the final step of <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d4fff554a316927771885dc8700abe\">heme</span> synthesis, where <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"ffb2e30f4b1692777202053635c365\">ferrous</span> iron is inserted into <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"510ec2d8ea1692777196c492eae686\">protoporphyrin</span> IX to <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"a1b06f401f1692777203a53393ba98\">form</span> heme.</p>\n<p><strong>Coproporphyrinogen <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"4a14dfa14e1692777194882f818d87\">oxidase</span> (Option D) </strong>is an <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"0f160e4e42169277718771b715516a\">enzyme</span> involved in the conversion of <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"11b250c1ba169277718522e7cde9a8\">coproporphyrinogen</span> III to <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"b6cbe38b7316927771961c7c1f5a00\">protoporphyrinogen</span> IX in the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d4fff554a316927771885dc8700abe\">heme</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"3fda45538a1692777199ec2a5478a5\">synthesis</span> pathway</p><br/><br/><div class=\"quiz-references\">Vasudevan Textbook of Biochemistry Edition 7th Pg. 276</div>","tags":""}]}